WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.460
- [Instructor] Welcome.

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.010
So let's see if we can figure out

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.040
what eight divided by 0.4 is.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.280
Pause this video and see if
you can work through that.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.150
All right.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.580
So we're trying to figure
out what eight ones

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.847
divided by four tenths is.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:18.430
And so one way to think about it

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.120
is to think about everything
in terms of tenths.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.820
So eight ones.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.670
One one is equal to 10 tenths,

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.070
so eight ones is equal to to 80 tenths.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.080
So this is equal to 80 tenths.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.820
And I'm dividing it by four tenths.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.090
So divided by four tenths.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.520
So if I have 80 tenths,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.010
and if I wanna divide it into
equal groups of four tenths,

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.020
how many equal groups am I going to have?

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.910
Well I am going to have 20
equal groups of four tenths.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.670
That would make up 80 tenths.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.990
80 divided by four is 20.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:00.400
So eight divided by four
tenths is equal to 20.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.160
Another way that we
could've approached that

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.960
is we could've thought about
it in terms of fractions.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.500
We could've said, hey, eight
divided by four tenths,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.880
that's the same thing as eight

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.400
divided by four tenths,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.070
which is the same thing when
you divide by a fraction.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:23.180
It's the same thing as
multiplying by the reciprocal.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.690
So this is the same thing as eight times

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.900
10 over four,

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.140
or you could view it as the
same thing as eight over one.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.660
Eight ones times 10 over four.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.760
Times 10 over four.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.330
In your numerator you get eight times 10,

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.350
so that is going to be equal to,

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.610
I'll do it in this orange color,

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.720
eight times 10 is equal to 80.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.060
And then in our denominator

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.870
we're going to have one times four.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.000
I didn't circle the one.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.340
You're going to have
the one times the four.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.280
So that's just going to be equal to four.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.030
So 80 fourths, or 80 divided by four,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.330
once again that is
going to be equal to 20.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.633
Let's do another example,
but in this case,

00:02:09.016 --> 00:02:10.390
let's deal with hundredths.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.920
So draw a line here.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.160
And so let's say that someone
walks up to you on the street

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.467
and says, "Quick,

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.847
"what is 48

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:20.570
"divided by

00:02:21.537 --> 00:02:23.027
"0.24?"

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.960
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.850
and I'll give you a little bit of a hint.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.660
The techniques we just did might apply.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.873
Although now we're
dealing with hundredths.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.470
All right now let's work on this together.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:39.950
Well one way to work on it
is you could view this as 48.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.500
You could just convert
everything to fractions.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.480
As 48, and actually I can
just write it as 48 over one,

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.990
divided by

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.620
divided by

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.817
24 hundredths

00:02:51.817 --> 00:02:54.290
24 hundredths.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.150
This division sign looks
a little bit weird.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.400
Let me make it look a
little bit more normal.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.260
There you go.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.030
And so when you divide by a fraction

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.070
that's the same thing as
multiplying by the reciprocal.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.510
We've seen that before.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.920
So this is equal to 48 over one

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.990
times 100 24ths.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.490
And so our numerator here

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.490
is going to be equal to 48 times 100.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.310
Actually I'm just gonna write
that out as 48 times 100

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.320
in the numerator.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.930
And then our denominator is
going to be 24 times one.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.390
Well that's just would equal to 24.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.660
And so what is this going to be equal to?

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.070
48 times 100 divided by 24.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.810
Well we could divide the numerator

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.960
and the denominator by 24.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.760
If we did that, 48 divided by 24 is two.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.400
And 24 divided by 24 is one,

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.410
so we're left with two
times 100 divided by one.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.520
Well two times 100 is equal to 200.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.070
And then you divide that
by one, you still get 200.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:57.903
So there you have it.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.990
This is equal to 200.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.670
Now another way that you
could have approached this

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.920
is you could've thought
about everything again,

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.780
in terms of hundredths.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.673
And so 48 ones is the same
thing as 4800 hundredths.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.893
So it's equal to 48.

00:04:18.151 --> 00:04:22.580
4800 hundredths.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.110
So let me write that down.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:24.943
Hundredths.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.960
Divided by 24 hundredths.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.210
Divided by 24 hundredths.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:39.210
So if I have 4800 or 4,800 hundredths,

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.410
and if I wanna divide it into
equal groups of 24 hundredths,

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.303
how many of those equal
groups would I have?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:52.180
Well you would have 4,800
divided by 24 equal groups.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.570
So this is going to be equal to

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.643
4,800.

00:04:57.643 --> 00:04:59.360
4,800.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.163
Divided by 24.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:05.450
Now 4,800 is exactly what we had up here.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.650
And so we already saw

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:11.180
that 4,800 divided by 24 is equal to 200.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.970
And if you just got to this point,

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.670
and if you said, hey,
how could I work on this?

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.200
You could just say, hey, let me divide

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.550
the numerator and the denominator by 24.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:23.550
You could try to re express
4800 as 48 times 100.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.890
Or you could even say
that 48 is 24 times two,

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.530
and then you're gonna
multiply that times 100

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:30.830
to get to 4,800.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.530
And then the division is a
little bit more straightforward.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.210
But the big picture here is to realize

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:39.920
that dividing by decimals
is not some mysterious thing

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.140
when you think about it
in terms of place value

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:45.493
or when you think about
it in terms of fractions.

